    "body": "Problem: The reuse_client predicate does not pass the target buffer, preventing decisions from being truly made per buffer.\r\n\r\nSolution: Pass the target buffer.\r\n\r\nCloses: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41162\r\n\r\n----------------\r\n\r\nThis is a non-breaking additional arg to avoid impact on nvim-lspconfig as well as the user config space. I'm willing to revise if this is not the right direction.",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-07T15:27:20Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks! The buffer sure seems relevant to `reuse_client`, but want to check with @neovim/lsp  @lewis6991 @mfussenegger if this is already possible somehow. I see that `start()` takes `opts.bufnr` but not sure if it's exposed to `reuse_client`.",
